course: french
lesson: 30
title: Questions and simple sentences
level: primary-4
stars: 3
explain: The easiest French question is an ordinary sentence with your voice going up at the end like a little hill: "Tu as un chien ?" - Do you have a dog?
explain: Another easy way is to put est-ce que, said "ess-kuh", at the front of a sentence: "Est-ce que tu aimes les chats ?"
explain: Then there are the question words: qui (who), quoi (what), où (where), quand (when), comment (how), pourquoi (why) and combien (how many) - with pourquoi always answered by parce que (because).
explain: Picture a beach in Brittany: you point at a crab and ask "Qu'est-ce que c'est ?", a French kid says "C'est un crabe !", and then "Tu as quel âge ?" - "J'ai dix ans, et toi ?"
explain: To say "not", sandwich the verb between ne and pas: je n'aime pas le foot, il n'est pas là.
fact: The easiest question is a normal sentence with the voice rising at the end: Tu as un chien ?
fact: Est-ce que at the start turns a sentence into a yes or no question; it sounds "ess-kuh".
fact: Qu'est-ce que c'est ? means "What is it?" and sounds "kess-kuh SAY"; the answer starts C'est un... or C'est une...
fact: The same question can be asked in several correct ways: Tu habites où ?, Où est-ce que tu habites ?, Où habites-tu ? (the last is more formal).
fact: Tu as quel âge ? means "How old are you?"; âge is masculine, so it is quel, not quelle; heure (hour) is feminine, so it is Quelle heure est-il ? (What time is it?).
fact: Ne goes before the verb and pas after it: je n'aime pas, il n'est pas là.
fact: Combien de + plural noun means "how many": combien de frères, combien de chats.
fact: Question words: qui (who), quoi (what), où (where), quand (when), comment (how), pourquoi (why), combien (how many).
fact: Pourquoi ? (why?) is answered with parce que (because): Parce que c'est génial !
fact: Comment s'appelle ton chien ? means "What is your dog called?"; the answer is Il s'appelle... or Elle s'appelle...
fact: People in Quebec speak French but are Canadian, so Tu viens d'où ? (Where are you from?) is safer than guessing.
exercise: Jack says "Tu as un chien" flatly and it sounds like a statement. What is the easiest fix? | Make his voice go up at the end | Say it louder and slower | Put pas after the verb | Add s'il te plaît at the end
exercise: How does est-ce que sound? | "ess-kuh" | "est-say-kway" | "ess-tay-KAY" | "es-KWAY-kuh"
exercise: What does est-ce que do at the start of a sentence? | Turns it into a yes or no question | Turns it into a "not" sentence | Turns it into a polite order | Turns it into the past tense
exercise: Archie points at a snail. What does he ask? | Qu'est-ce que c'est ? | Où est-ce que c'est ? | Quand est-ce que c'est ? | Qui est-ce que c'est ?
exercise: Which is NOT a correct way to ask where someone lives? | Où tu habites est-ce que ? | Tu habites où ? | Où est-ce que tu habites ? | Où habites-tu ?
exercise: How do you ask "How old are you?" | Tu as quel âge ? | Tu es quel âge ? | Tu as quelle âge ? | Quel tu as âge ?
exercise: Why is it quel âge and not quelle âge? | Âge is a masculine word | Âge starts with a vowel | Quelle is only for questions about time | Quel is always used before nouns
exercise: Jayden writes "Je aime pas". What is right? | Je n'aime pas | Je ne pas aime | Je aime ne pas | Je n'aime pas pas
exercise: Lily wants to know how many brothers. What does she ask? | Combien de frères tu as ? | Combien frères tu as ? | Quand de frères tu as ? | Combien des frère tu as ?
exercise: Which word means "when"? | quand | qui | quoi | comment
exercise: Which word means "how"? | comment | combien | pourquoi | quand
exercise: Oscar asks "Pourquoi tu aimes le rugby ?" How does the answer start? | Parce que... | Pourquoi... | Comment... | Quand...
exercise: Isla asks "Comment s'appelle ton chien ?" What does she want to know? | The dog's name | How old the dog is | Where the dog lives | How the dog is feeling
exercise: Max's new classmate speaks French and is from Quebec. What is the safest question? | Tu viens d'où ? | Tu es français ? | Tu es anglais ? | Tu parles français ?
exercise: Which question word means "who"? | qui | quoi | quand | où
test: ★★★ Leo's friend says "J'ai dix ans, et toi ?" Leo is one year younger. What does he answer? | J'ai neuf ans | Je suis neuf ans | Moi, j'ai onze ans | Moi, je suis neuf
test: Your mate goes, "Est-ce que? Just say every letter, est-say-kway, bruv." What's right? | It's said "ess-kuh" | He's right, every letter is said | It's said "es-tee-say" | It's said "kway" on its own
test: ★★★ A penpal writes: "J'ai deux sœurs et un frère." Lily asks "Combien de frères et sœurs tu as ?" What is the answer in numbers? | 3 | 2 | 1 | 4
test: ★★★ Which question would a French person NOT answer with parce que? | Combien de chats tu as ? | Pourquoi tu aimes le foot ? | Pourquoi tu es triste ? | Pourquoi tu ris ?
test: Ruby from Galway goes, "Ah sure, there's only one right way to ask where you live, yeah?" What's true? | Several are right, like Tu habites où ? and Où habites-tu ? | Only Où habites-tu ? is ever correct | Only Tu habites où ? is ever correct | Only Où est-ce que tu habites ? works
test: A cartoon kid says "Je pas aime ne les maths." Your sister says, "That's well wonky." Fix it. | Je n'aime pas les maths | Je ne pas aime les maths | J'aime ne pas les maths | Je aime pas ne les maths
test: ★★★ Match: "Comment ?", "Où ?", "Quand ?" | How, where, when | When, where, how | Where, how, when | How, when, who
test: Max from Toronto asks his classmate "Tu es français ?" and gets "Non, je suis québécois !" He goes, "Oops, eh." What did he forget? | French is spoken in Quebec, in Canada, not only in France | Quebec is a city in France | Québécois is a type of French food | People in Quebec speak only English
test: ★★★ Which answer fits the question "Qu'est-ce que c'est ?" | C'est un escargot | Il s'appelle Biscuit | J'ai dix ans | J'habite à Lyon
test: What would happen if you asked "Tu aimes les chats" with your voice going down at the end? | It might sound like you're telling them they like cats | It would sound rude and they'd walk off | It would mean "you hate cats" | Nothing, the voice never matters
test: Your US cousin says, "No cap, quel is for everything, so quel âge, quel heure." (no cap = honestly) Which is true? | Quel âge is right, but heure is feminine: quelle heure | He's right, quel goes with every word | Both are wrong: quelle âge, quelle heure | Both are wrong: quel âges, quel heures
exam: Identify the expression which, placed at the commencement of a statement, renders it interrogative. | Est-ce que | Parce que | Ne ... pas | Il y a
exam: Select the correct rendering of the question "How old are you?" addressed to a child. | Tu as quel âge ? | Tu es quel âge ? | Tu as quelle âge ? | Quel âge tu es ?
exam: Determine the conjunction with which a question introduced by pourquoi is customarily answered. | parce que | pourquoi | quand | comment
exam: Ascertain the position of the elements ne and pas in relation to the verb in a negative statement. | ne before the verb, pas after it | both before the verb | both after the verb | pas before the verb, ne after it
